sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  %% Participants
  participant Operator as Operator / ch-remote
  participant HTTP as HTTP API thread
  participant VMM as VMM control loop (Vmm)
  participant HYP as Hypervisor (KVM / MSHV)
  participant MM as MemoryManager
  participant UFFD as UFFD handler thread
  participant KERNEL as Linux kernel (/dev/userfaultfd, memfd, ioctls)
  participant DM as DeviceManager
  participant VCPU as vCPU threads
  participant MIGWORK as MigrationWorker (sender)
  participant MIGDST as Migration Destination / Restore Source
  participant POST as Postcopy server / page-source worker

  Note over VMM,HTTP: Cloud-Hypervisor process start
  Operator->>VMM: Start CH process (binary)
  VMM->>VMM: Initialize runtime, apply seccomp and landlock, start threads
  VMM->>HTTP: Spawn HTTP API thread
  VMM->>DM: Initialize DeviceManager (deferred device creation until boot)
  Note right of HTTP: /vmm.ping becomes answerable once API thread is up

  %% vmm.ping
  Operator->>HTTP: GET /vmm.ping
  HTTP->>VMM: ApiRequest(VmmPing)
  VMM-->>HTTP: VmmPingResponse(build_version, version, pid, features)
  HTTP-->>Operator: 200 OK (VMM info)

  %% vm.create
  Operator->>HTTP: PUT /vm.create (VmConfig JSON)
  HTTP->>VMM: ApiRequest(VmCreate, VmConfig)
  VMM->>VMM: Store VmConfig (cold)
  HTTP-->>Operator: 204 No Content

  %% vm.boot (main boot flow)
  Operator->>HTTP: PUT /vm.boot
  HTTP->>VMM: ApiRequest(VmBoot)
  VMM->>VMM: Pre-boot validation, create consoles
  VMM->>HYP: KVM_CREATE_VM (hypervisor VM)
  Note over VMM,HYP: Apply hypervisor ioctls (KVM_SET_* etc.)

  alt Memory: eager / normal
    VMM->>MM: Create guest memory (mmap / file-backed)
    MM->>HYP: KVM_SET_USER_MEMORY_REGION (register regions with KVM)
  else Memory: memfd (shared memory / migration)
    VMM->>KERNEL: Create memfd objects (memfd_create)
    KERNEL-->>VMM: Return memfd FDs
    VMM->>HYP: Attach memfd-backed memory (KVM / memfd path)
  else Memory: restore / on-demand (userfaultfd)
    VMM->>MIGDST: Receive snapshot metadata and memory ranges (transport)
    MIGDST-->>VMM: Memory metadata, snapshot file / memfds / fault socket info
    VMM->>KERNEL: Open /dev/userfaultfd or userfaultfd(2) using USERFAULTFD_IOC_NEW
    KERNEL-->>VMM: Return uffd FD
    VMM->>KERNEL: ioctl(UFFDIO_API) - announce features and ioctls
    VMM->>KERNEL: ioctl(UFFDIO_REGISTER, ranges, UFFDIO_REGISTER_MODE_MISSING)
    VMM->>UFFD: Spawn UFFD handler thread with a copy of the uffd FD
    VMM->>MM: Create MemoryManager with snapshot metadata (defer page population)
  end

  %% Device creation and registration
  VMM->>DM: Instantiate devices (virtio-net/block, VFIO, vhost-user backends)
  DM->>HYP: Register irqfds / ioeventfds, map BARs, set KVM device attributes

  alt vhost-user devices
    DM->>POST: Spawn vhost-user backend process (optional)
  end

  %% vCPU creation and booting
  VMM->>HYP: KVM_CREATE_VCPU (per vCPU)
  HYP-->>VMM: Return vCPU file descriptors
  VMM->>VCPU: Spawn vCPU threads (one per vCPU)
  VCPU->>HYP: KVM_RUN (enter guest execution)
  VMM->>DM: Activate virtio devices
  VMM->>VMM: Set VM state = Running
  HTTP-->>Operator: 204 No Content (vm.boot accepted)
  Note over VCPU,MM: With UFFD on-demand restore, the guest may block on first access while a page is fetched

  %% UFFD fault handling (on-demand restore)
  Note over UFFD,KERNEL: UFFD handler runs in the background
  KERNEL->>UFFD: On guest page fault, write uffd_msg to the uffd FD
  UFFD->>UFFD: Read struct uffd_msg (UFFD_EVENT_PAGEFAULT)
  UFFD->>MIGDST: Request page data through fault socket / transport (page request with GPA)
  MIGDST-->>UFFD: Return page payload (page bytes)
  UFFD->>KERNEL: ioctl(UFFDIO_COPY, dst=guest_addr, src=buf, len)
  UFFD->>KERNEL: ioctl(UFFDIO_WAKE or UFFDIO_CONTINUE) to wake blocked threads

  alt Page cannot be provided / error
    UFFD->>KERNEL: ioctl(UFFDIO_POISON) or UFFDIO_ZEROPAGE, depending on policy
    Note right of UFFD: On older kernels, some operations may fail and restore may abort
  end

  %% Query: restoring state and API reflection
  Note over VMM: VMM exposes MemoryManager::restoring() while UFFD handling or prefaulting is incomplete
  Operator->>HTTP: GET /vm.info
  HTTP->>VMM: ApiRequest(VmInfo)
  VMM-->>HTTP: VmInfoResponse(state=Running/Created, memory_actual_size, device_tree)
  HTTP-->>Operator: 200 OK

  %% Migration: high-level send side
  Operator->>HTTP: PUT /vm.send-migration (destination_url, memory_mode)
  HTTP->>VMM: ApiRequest(VmSendMigration)
  VMM->>MIGWORK: Spawn MigrationWorker thread (take VM ownership)
  MIGWORK->>MIGDST: transport::send_migration_socket(connect)
  MIGWORK->>MIGDST: Send Request::start()

  alt Memory mode: precopy
    MIGWORK->>VMM: Iterate memory rounds (send dirty pages while VM runs)
    loop Memory iteration
      MIGWORK->>MIGDST: Send memory ranges for iteration
      MIGDST-->>MIGWORK: Acknowledge iteration
    end
    MIGWORK->>VMM: Pause VM for final iteration
    MIGWORK->>MIGDST: Send final snapshot and state
  else Memory mode: memfds
    MIGWORK->>MIGDST: Send memfd FDs through SCM_RIGHTS over Unix socket
  else Memory mode: postcopy
    MIGWORK->>MIGDST: Open postcopy fault connection (fault_stream)
    MIGDST->>MIGWORK: Destination registers UFFD and sends page faults over fault_stream
    MIGWORK->>POST: Spawn postcopy serving thread
    loop Page-fault requests from destination
      POST->>MIGWORK: Request guest memory pages and send them
    end
  end

  %% FD passing (SCM_RIGHTS) for memfds, VFIO cdev, iommufd
  Note over MIGWORK,MIGDST: Send or receive memfd, VFIO cdev, and iommufd FDs using SCM_RIGHTS over Unix domain sockets
  MIGWORK->>MIGDST: Send memfd / vfio_fds / iommufd_fd using SCM_RIGHTS

  %% Post-migration completion
  MIGDST->>MIGWORK: Send Request::complete acknowledgment
  MIGWORK->>VMM: Release VM ownership if preserve_source=false, or preserve according to flags
  VMM->>VMM: If moved, stop local VM or continue according to preserve_source

  %% Thread and failure notes
  Note over VMM: Concurrent threads:<br/>HTTP API thread(s)<br/>VMM control-loop thread<br/>vCPU threads (one per vCPU)<br/>UFFD handler thread(s) for on-demand restore<br/>MigrationWorker and its TCP, worker, and postcopy threads<br/>Event-monitor, signal-handler, and GDB threads (optional)

  Note over KERNEL: Kernel version and permission constraints:<br/>/dev/userfaultfd requires Linux 6.1+ for the device node<br/>Some UFFD features and poison operations require newer kernels, such as Linux 6.6+<br/>The userfaultfd(2) syscall may be restricted by vm.unprivileged_userfaultfd<br/>Misconfigured seccomp or landlock rules may block necessary operations

  %% End
  Note over Operator,VMM: VM is running guest boot progress is observed from inside the guest through cloud-init, serial console, or an agent